research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-60-{"id":"cex-limit-differs-from-the-value","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classification_of_discontinuities","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_limoffunc.html"],"rationale":"The sources give the standard removable-discontinuity construction in which changing one value leaves the punctured limit unchanged. The local witness fixes values 0 and 1 and also computes both one-sided limits.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl:61:{"id":"cex-composition-of-limits-fails","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_limoffunc.html","https://terrytao.wordpress.com/books/analysis-i/"],"rationale":"The standard caveat in composition of limits is exactly that an inner function may equal L where the outer value differs from its limit. The local example instantiates it with a constant inner function and the preceding removable defect.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-62-{"id":"cex-dirichlet-has-no-limit-anywhere","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirichlet_function"],"rationale":"The source defines the rational indicator and states that it is discontinuous everywhere because rationals and irrationals are dense. The local item restates this as nonexistence of every punctured limit and proves that semantically equivalent form with rational and irrational sequences.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-63-{"id":"ex-x-times-dirichlet-has-a-limit-only-at-zero","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirichlet_function","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squeeze_theorem"],"rationale":"The modified Dirichlet function x on rationals and 0 on irrationals is the standard example continuous only at zero. The local item phrases this as existence of a punctured limit exactly at zero and proves it by squeeze plus two dense sequences.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
