research/audit/wave7-proof-contracts.json:14014:        "notes": "critical risk (13): 9 declared dependencies; 9 cited facts; 10 numbered proof steps; existence, choice, uniqueness, or well-definedness; boundary-sensitive language; analytic limiting/completeness language, routed by risk-report.mjs. The read-only DeepSeek V4 Pro audit-refuter received the complete target and every cited dependency and returned CLEAN. Boundary evidence: The counterexample uses the distinct reals 0 and 1 (L5) and the fact that 0 is a limit point of ℝ (L2). The limits of f, g, and f∘g at 0 all exist under the ε-δ definition because c=0 is a limit point of the domain ℝ and the required inequalities hold for every positive ε. No empty domain, degenerate interval, or nonempty‑choice issue arises. The proof contract’s boundary checks (zero, one, degenerate, nonempty‑choice) are satisfied; endpoint and biconditional cases are not applicable. Checked surface: The title, the public claim (the refuted statement and the counterexample description), every numbered step (1.1 through 5.1), and the Remarks were read and found mathematically accurate. ``` Alpha adjudicated the return against the current item and cited dependencies on disk and found no fatal mathematical or dependency-citation defect. Evidence: research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/cex-composition-of-limits-fails--48b355091e250bcc.result.json."
